+# Passkey account integration
+
+This repository is a static site without authentication or an account API. By default, the account screen displays clearly labeled sample data. Sample changes use browser local storage and never signal an authenticator.
+
+To connect the UI, supply `window.dailyGrindPasskeys` before the inline account script. The service must expose:
+
+- `list(): Promise<Passkey[]>` — list only the signed-in customer's registered passkeys.
+- `rename(id, name): Promise<void>` — persist a trimmed account label (1–60 characters).
+- `remove(id): Promise<RemovalResult>` — revoke the credential on the server and return the authoritative remaining credential list. Reject on failure.
+
+A `Passkey` has `id`, `name`, `device` (`laptop`, `phone`, or `usb`), `provider`, `created`, `lastUsed`, optional `current`, and `credentialId` (the actual base64url WebAuthn credential ID). Dates are display strings. `current` should only be set when the current credential is known.
+
+`RemovalResult` has `rpId`, `userId` (base64url WebAuthn user handle), and `acceptedCredentialIds` (the complete remaining list of base64url credential IDs, including an empty list after the last removal).
+
+The UI calls `PublicKeyCredential.signalAllAcceptedCredentials` after successful server revocation. Where only `signalUnknownCredential` is supported, it signals the removed credential instead. If neither method is available, metadata is missing, or the signal fails, the customer receives manual removal guidance. Signal completion means the authenticator was notified; it does not prove removal on every synced device. Renaming changes an account label, not the WebAuthn username or display name.
+
+The host service must enforce session authentication, passkey ownership, CSRF protection, input validation, and any required reauthentication or alternative sign-in checks before removing the last passkey. Never supply session tokens or real credentials through local storage. Connected records stay in memory and failures do not fall back to sample records.
+
+Reference: [WebAuthn credential signals](https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn/#sctn-signal-credential-state).
+
+Verification: inline JavaScript syntax and isolated interaction checks; no development/preview server or browser verification.
